If a patient receives a methadone-treatment for an opioid-use-disorder and requires an additional-opioid for a severe-acute-pain then every clinician should use a careful-monitoring for the patient.
If a patient receives a methadone-treatment for an opioid-use-disorder and requires an additional-opioid for a severe-acute-pain and a pain-care-clinician-treatment is feasible then the patient should receive the pain-care-clinician-treatment with an opioid-treatment-program-consultation.
